A carve that checks the block's size but not where it starts
hands out a range no single NAPOT entry describes:
a power of two at an offset that is not a multiple of it.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-grain32 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: region capability is not a NAPOT block

diff --git a/kernel/syscall.c b/kernel/syscall.c
--- a/kernel/syscall.c
+++ b/kernel/syscall.c
@@ -125,7 +125,7 @@ static int op_region(struct thread *t, uint32_t slot, const struct cap *cap,
         uint32_t off = arg[1];
         uint32_t len = arg[2];
         /* A block within the region, so that every region capability is one NAPOT entry. */
-        if (off >= size || len > size - off || !napot_block(base + off, len)) {
+        if (off >= size || len > size - off || !napot_block(base, len)) {
             return KERR_INVALID_ARG;
         }
         struct cap sub = cap_to_region(base + off, len, cap->rights);
